From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:25:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: write the HDMI power
 enables as the ADT does

The J604 ADT drives the HDMI port's power enables through SMC write
templates: function-hdmi_pwr_en is pKW4("gP0f", 0x00800000) and
function-dp2hdmi_pwr_en is pKW4("gP1a", 0x0), with the level in the low
bits. Without a template, gpio-macsmc writes these lines with its generic
CMD_OUTPUT command instead, which the SMC is not known to latch for them;
the J604's gP13 already needed its template for the same reason.

Describe both lines with apple,output-templates, as the T6050 boards do
for the same two lines, so the HDMI path writes exactly what the ADT
asks for.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 0549485d29..f47f505c6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -324,6 +324,12 @@ &port02 {
 &smc_gpio {
 	interrupt-controller;
 	#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+	/*
+	 * The HDMI port's power enables, as the ADT's function-hdmi_pwr_en
+	 * (gP0f) and function-dp2hdmi_pwr_en (gP1a) write them: a four-byte
+	 * template with the level in its low bits.
+	 */
+	apple,output-templates = <0x0f 0x00800000>, <0x1a 0x00000000>;
 };
 
